# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 75-76 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 10 — CHAPTER 12, 2026-09-20; the one run): the border enlarged and the slaughter as
# commanded (75), the blood (76) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch12_ink.SP_; the middah where the row argues by one (checked in
# MIDDOT.md before it was typed). Chapter 11's form.
from ch12_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(75, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD ENLARGES YOUR BORDER" (12:20) — DO THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE CONTEXT, FOR AS ITS REWARD THE LORD WILL ENLARGE YOUR BORDER. The head row of piska 75 ({SP_(75, 1, "עשה", "מצוה", "האמורה", "בענין")} "do the commandment said in the context"): the "when" a reward conditional (80:1 the same form); THE INK: the clause 12:20 alone, 19:8 its defective twin (computed). Fresh.')
srow(75, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS HE SPOKE TO YOU" — WHAT DID HE SPEAK TO YOU? THE LAND OF THE KENITE, THE KENIZZITE AND THE KADMONITE (GENESIS 15:19). RABBI: THOSE ARE ALREADY SAID; WHAT DID HE SPEAK? "FROM THE EAST SIDE TO THE WEST, DAN ONE … JUDAH ONE, ASHER ONE" (EZEKIEL 48:1-7). THE AS_WHEN RECEIPT\'S CALLEE ({SP_(75, 2, "מה", "דבר", "לך")} "what did He speak to you"; {SP_(75, 2, "כבר", "אלו", "אמורים")} "these are already said"): a DISPUTE on the pointer\'s target — the covenant of the pieces (Genesis 15:18-21, the three nations beyond the seven) or Ezekiel 48\'s tribal strips; the Mekhilta Pischa 18 parallel (the English); the design\'s RUN_CITATION pointer for 10b\'s census (12:20 the AS_WHEN form — computed). Read before at two Genesis sittings (the ledgers hold 75:2 on Genesis 15), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(75, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SAY: LET ME EAT FLESH, FOR YOUR SOUL CRAVES TO EAT FLESH" — R. ISHMAEL: IT TELLS THAT THE FLESH OF DESIRE WAS FORBIDDEN TO ISRAEL IN THE WILDERNESS, AND WHEN THEY CAME TO THE LAND THE VERSE PERMITTED IT. THE RELEASE FROM LEVITICUS 17 NAMED ({SP_(75, 3, "מגיד", "שבשר", "תאוה", "נאסר", "להם", "לישראל", "במדבר")} "it tells that the flesh of desire was forbidden to Israel in the wilderness"): R. Ishmael reads 12:20 as the repeal of Leviticus 17:3-4\'s "every slaughter at the tent" on entering the Land — THE INK: Leviticus 17:3-5 shares one token in order with 12:15 (computed), the release said in new words; Chullin 16b-17a the dispute with R. Akiva at 10b — THE COMPILE\'S QUESTION: a law changed by a place (the tape\'s entry into the land the switch). Fresh.')
srow(75, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: THE VERSE COMES ONLY TO TEACH YOU THE COMMANDMENTS SAID IN IT. ({SP_(75, 4, "לא", "בא", "הכתוב", "אלא", "ללמדך", "מצוות", "האמורות", "בו")} "the verse comes only to teach you the commandments said in it"): the counter-reading — no repeal, the wilderness\'s flesh of desire never forbidden, the verse teaches the slaughter\'s law (Chullin 17a); no citation in either file; a DISPUTE row. Fresh.')
srow(75, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELAZAR BEN AZARIAH: THE VERSE COMES ONLY TO TEACH GOOD CONDUCT — A MAN EATS FLESH ONLY OUT OF APPETITE. MIGHT HE BUY FROM THE MARKET AND EAT? "YOU SHALL SLAUGHTER OF YOUR HERD AND YOUR FLOCK" (12:21) — A MAN EATS NO FLESH UNTIL HE HAS HERD AND FLOCK; MIGHT HE SLAUGHTER ALL HIS FLOCK AND HERD? "OF YOUR HERD" — NOT ALL YOUR HERD; "OF YOUR FLOCK" — NOT ALL YOUR FLOCK. THE CIVILITY READING ({SP_(75, 5, "ללמדך", "דרך", "ארץ")} "to teach you good conduct"; {SP_(75, 5, "מבקרך", "ולא", "כל", "בקרך")} "of your herd and not all your herd"): the partitive "of" a PARAMETER of measure — Tosefta Arakhin 4:26 (the English); Chullin 84a at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(75, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS I HAVE COMMANDED YOU" (12:21) — AS HOLY THINGS BY SLAUGHTER, SO COMMON BY SLAUGHTER. THE RECEIPT WITHOUT THE NAME READ ({SP_(75, 6, "מה", "קדשים", "בשחיטה", "אף", "חולין", "בשחיטה")} "as holy things by slaughter, so common by slaughter"): "as I commanded you" pointed at the rite of slaughter taught for the offerings — the shelf names the callee; THE INK: the phrase\'s one kin Exodus 23:15 (computed), the register\'s finder blind to it (measured — the third form owed since 4b, its fourth seat). Fresh; Chullin 28a at 10b.')
srow(75, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'OR AS HOLY THINGS IN THE PLACE, SO COMMON IN THE PLACE? "WHEN THE PLACE IS FAR" — AT A DISTANCE YOU SLAUGHTER, NOT NEAR THE PLACE: TO EXCLUDE COMMON ANIMALS SLAUGHTERED IN THE COURT. ({SP_(75, 7, "ברחוק", "מקום", "אתה", "זובח")} "at a distance from the place you slaughter"; {SP_(75, 7, "פרט", "לחולין", "שנשחטו", "בעזרה")} "to exclude common animals slaughtered in the court"): the comparison bounded — the place a PARAMETER (common slaughter forbidden in the court; Kiddushin 57b at 10b). Fresh.')
srow(75, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY UNBLEMISHED? BLEMISHED WHENCE? "HE SHALL SLAUGHTER IT AT THE DOOR OF THE TENT OF MEETING" (LEVITICUS 3:2). MIGHT EVEN A WILD ANIMAL OR A BIRD AT THE DOOR? "IT" (LEVITICUS 3:8) — IT, NOT A WILD ANIMAL OR A BIRD. ({SP_(75, 8, "אותו", "פתח", "אהל", "מועד")} "it at the door of the tent of meeting"): Leviticus 3 (read) called for the blemished and the excluded kinds — Sifra Nedavah 17:7-9 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(75, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'OR AS HOLY THINGS WITHIN A TIME, SO COMMON WITHIN A TIME? "YOU SHALL EAT IN YOUR GATES WITH ALL THE DESIRE OF YOUR SOUL." ({SP_(75, 9, "מה", "קדשים", "בזמן", "אף", "חולין", "בזמן")} "as holy things within a time, so common within a time"): the comparison bounded — no time limit. Fresh.')
srow(75, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'OR WITHIN A PARTITION? "IN YOUR GATES." OR BY DAY? "IN YOUR GATES WITH ALL THE DESIRE OF YOUR SOUL." ({SP_(75, 10, "מה", "קדשים", "ביום", "אף", "חולין", "ביום")} "as holy things by day, so common by day"): two more bounds — no partition, no daylight rule. Fresh.')
srow(75, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'OR IN CLEANNESS? "THE UNCLEAN MAY EAT" (12:22). ONLY THE UNCLEAN? THE CLEAN WHENCE? "THE CLEAN MAY EAT." "THE UNCLEAN AND THE CLEAN TOGETHER" — BOTH EAT FROM ONE DISH. MIGHT EVEN THE HEAVE OFFERING? "TOGETHER THEY SHALL EAT IT" — THIS, NOT THE HEAVE OFFERING. ({SP_(75, 11, "מלמד", "ששניהם", "אוכלים", "מתוך", "קערה", "אחת")} "it teaches that both eat from one dish"): 71:7-8 said again of the common flesh (there of the redeemed) — the fifth bound; Tosefta Niddah 9:18 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(75, 12, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT THEY BE LIABLE FOR THE BREAST AND THIGH? "AS THE GAZELLE" (12:15). ({SP_(75, 12, "יכול", "יהו", "חיבים", "בחזה", "ושוק")} "might they be liable for the breast and thigh"): 71:9-10 again, of the common flesh (Leviticus 7:31-32 — the English). Fresh.')
srow(75, 13, 'CONTEXT', f'SHALL I EXCLUDE FROM THE BREAST AND THIGH AND NOT FROM THE TWO KIDNEYS AND THE LOBE OF THE LIVER? "AS THE HART." ({SP_(75, 13, "שתי", "כליות", "ויותרת", "הכבד")} "the two kidneys and the lobe of the liver"): Leviticus 3:4-5\'s parts. Fresh.')
srow(75, 14, 'CONTEXT', f'OR AS THE GAZELLE IS WHOLLY PERMITTED, SO THIS? "BUT" (12:22). ({SP_(75, 14, "תלמוד", "לומר", "אך")} "the Teaching states: but"): the fat of common cattle still forbidden — 71:11 again with "but" for "only". Fresh.')
srow(75, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"BUT AS THE GAZELLE AND THE HART ARE EATEN" (12:22) — R. ELAZAR HA-KAPPAR: WHAT DOES THE VERSE TEACH BETWEEN GAZELLE AND HART? IT COMES TO TEACH AND IS FOUND TAUGHT: AS THE DOMESTIC ANIMAL BY SLAUGHTER, SO THE WILD ANIMAL BY SLAUGHTER; BUT THE BIRD ONLY BY THE WORDS OF THE SCRIBES. RABBI: "AS I HAVE COMMANDED YOU" — IT TELLS THAT MOSES WAS COMMANDED ON THE GULLET AND THE WINDPIPE, THE GREATER PART OF ONE FOR A BIRD, THE GREATER PART OF TWO FOR A BEAST. THE SLAUGHTER\'S RULES FROM THE RECEIPT ({SP_(75, 15, "הרי", "זה", "בא", "ללמד", "ונמצא", "למד")} "this comes to teach and is found taught"; {SP_(75, 15, "מגיד", "שנצטוה", "משה", "על", "הושט", "ועל", "הגרגרת")} "it tells that Moses was commanded on the gullet and the windpipe"): the comes-to-teach-and-is-taught move (named by the row; the thirty-two\'s scope move) — the wild animal\'s slaughter from the comparison, the bird\'s from the scribes; Rabbi\'s reading makes 12:21\'s receipt THE ORAL LAW\'S SEAT — the rules of slaughter given to Moses and written nowhere: Mishnah Chullin 2:1 the answer sheet (the English), Chullin 28a at 10b; the translator\'s doubt on the parallel (the English). Fresh.')

srow(76, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY BE STEADFAST NOT TO EAT THE BLOOD" (12:23) — R. JUDAH: IT TELLS THAT ISRAEL WERE STEEPED IN BLOOD BEFORE THE GIVING OF THE TORAH. The head row of piska 76 ({SP_(76, 1, "שישראל", "שטופים", "בדם", "קודם", "מתן", "תורה")} "that Israel were steeped in blood before the giving of the Torah"): "be steadfast" read as evidence of habit — the word said to Joshua said to the eater (THE INK: the imperative\'s four seats in the book, computed). Fresh.')
srow(76, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE EVEN AFTER THEY RECEIVED IT WITH JOY AT SINAI? "ONLY." R. SHIMON BEN AZZAI: ARE THERE NOT THREE HUNDRED POSITIVE COMMANDMENTS LIKE THIS IN THE TORAH? — AS THE BLOOD, THAN WHICH NO COMMANDMENT IS LIGHTER, THE VERSE WARNED YOU OF, THE REST OF THE COMMANDMENTS HOW MUCH MORE. ({SP_(76, 2, "שלש", "מאות", "מצוות", "עשה", "בתורה")} "three hundred positive commandments in the Torah"; {SP_(76, 2, "שאין", "בכל", "המצוות", "קל", "ממנו")} "than which none of the commandments is lighter"): I1 (checked) from the lightest; Mishnah Makkot 3:15 (the English; 76:9 and 286:16 say it again); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(76, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: EVERY COMMANDMENT ISRAEL RECEIVED WITH JOY AT SINAI THEY DO WITH JOY, AND EVERY ONE THEY DID NOT, THEY DO NOT DO WITH JOY. RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: EVERY COMMANDMENT FOR WHICH ISRAEL GAVE THEIR LIVES IN THE PERSECUTION THEY KEEP OPENLY; EVERY ONE THEY DID NOT DIE FOR IS STILL LOOSE IN THEIR HANDS. ({SP_(76, 3, "בשעת", "השמד")} "in the hour of the persecution"): the row\'s history — Sanhedrin 74a-b at 10b; no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(76, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"FOR THE BLOOD IS THE LIFE" — TO TELL WHAT CAUSED IT. ({SP_(76, 4, "להגיד", "מה", "גרם")} "to tell what caused it"): the reason clause read as a reason. Fresh.')
srow(76, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL NOT EAT THE LIFE WITH THE FLESH" — THIS IS A LIMB FROM THE LIVING. IS IT NOT REASONED? FLESH IN MILK, PERMITTED TO THE SONS OF NOAH, IS FORBIDDEN TO ISRAEL; A LIMB FROM THE LIVING, FORBIDDEN TO THE SONS OF NOAH, ALL THE MORE. THE BEAUTIFUL CAPTIVE AND HER LIKE REFUTE IT — FORBIDDEN TO THE SONS OF NOAH, PERMITTED TO ISRAEL; SO DO NOT WONDER AT THE LIMB: "YOU SHALL NOT EAT THE LIFE WITH THE FLESH" — THE LIMB FROM THE LIVING. THE A FORTIORI REFUTED, THE VERSE NEEDED ({SP_(76, 5, "זה", "אבר", "מן", "החי")} "this is a limb from the living"; {SP_(76, 5, "יפת", "תאר", "וכל", "הדומים", "לה", "תוכיח")} "the beautiful captive and all like her refute it"): I1 (checked) refuted by a counter-instance — the seven laws\' limb (Genesis 9:4 the kin, no token shared — computed); Chullin 102b at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(76, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'R. HANANIAH BEN GAMLIEL: THIS IS THE BLOOD FROM THE LIVING. ({SP_(76, 6, "זה", "הדם", "מן", "החי")} "this is the blood from the living"): Tosefta Avodah Zarah 8:6 (the English); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(76, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT EAT IT" (12:24) — TO INCLUDE FLESH IN MILK. IS IT NOT REASONED? CARRION, NOT LIABLE FOR ITS COOKING, LIABLE FOR ITS EATING; FLESH IN MILK, LIABLE FOR ITS COOKING, ALL THE MORE FOR ITS EATING. MIXED SEEDS REFUTE IT — LIABLE FOR THE SOWING, NOT FOR THE EATING; SO: "YOU SHALL NOT EAT IT" — FLESH IN MILK. ({SP_(76, 7, "לרבות", "בשר", "בחלב")} "to include flesh in milk"; {SP_(76, 7, "כלאי", "זרעים", "יוכיחו")} "mixed seeds refute it"): E1 (checked) after I1 (checked) refuted — 12:24\'s "it" made the third prohibition of flesh in milk (14:21 ahead; Chullin 115b at 10b); Mishnah Kilayim 8:1 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(76, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ELIEZER: THE PASSOVER OFFERING, NOT LIABLE FOR ITS COOKING, LIABLE FOR ITS EATING; FLESH IN MILK ALL THE MORE. THE COMPOUNDING OF THE INCENSE REFUTES — LIABLE FOR THE COMPOUNDING, NOT FOR THE SMELLING; SO "YOU SHALL NOT EAT IT" — FLESH IN MILK. ({SP_(76, 8, "פטום", "הקטרת", "יוכיח")} "the compounding of the incense refutes it"): I1 (checked) refuted by a second counter-instance. Fresh.')
srow(76, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'RABBAN GAMLIEL SON OF RABBI: "ONLY BE STEADFAST NOT TO EAT THE BLOOD" — AS THE BLOOD, THAN WHICH NONE IS LIGHTER, THE VERSE WARNED OF, THE REST HOW MUCH MORE (76:2 again). ({SP_(76, 9, "שאר", "כל", "המצוות", "על", "אחת", "כמה", "וכמה")} "the rest of the commandments how much more"): I1 (checked); Mishnah Makkot 3:15. Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(75, r) for r in range(1, 16)] + [(76, r) for r in range(1, 10)], sorted(S)
